\subsection{Return to the original arithmetic criterion}
The original TWA equality remains
\begin{equation}
 \mathcal B_k^{\rm ar}=\mathcal B_k^0+(R_k^0-R_k^\sigma)+\delta_k^\sigma.
\end{equation}
The complete original source deficits give the exact signed allowances
\begin{equation}
 a_k^-:=\Xi_{k,q-1}+\Xi_{k,q},\qquad
 a_k^+:=\Xi_{k,2q-1}+\Xi_{k,2q},\qquad
 -a_k^-\le\delta_k^\sigma\le a_k^+.
\end{equation}
The sign proof is the original nonnegative quotient-deficit identity
$\delta_k^\sigma=-b_{q-1}-b_q+b_{2q-1}+b_{2q}$ with
$0\le b_N\le\Xi_{k,N}$. It retains both low and both high cutoffs.
The complete finite expressions JSR17--20 in the receiving proof give
$\Xi_{k,N}\le kq\Omega_{k,N}^{\rm deg}$ and
\begin{equation}
 D_k^-:=kq(\Omega_{k,q-1}^{\rm deg}+\Omega_{k,q}^{\rm deg}),\qquad
 D_k^+:=kq(\Omega_{k,2q-1}^{\rm deg}+\Omega_{k,2q}^{\rm deg}),\qquad
 a_k^\pm\le D_k^\pm.
\end{equation}
Here $\Omega_{k,N}^{\rm deg}$ is the explicitly displayed scalar
original-degree majorant in JSR18; it is unrelated in type to the
positive matrix $\Omega_N$ above. All its source integrals and constants
are given in JSR17, and its complete substitution proof follows there.

If $[L_k,U_k]$ is the certificate \eqref{eq:cert}, the current arithmetic
receiver is
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{\begin{aligned}
 \mathcal B_k^0+L_k-a_k^-&\le\mathcal B_k^{\rm ar}
                         \le\mathcal B_k^0+U_k+a_k^+,\\
 \mathcal B_k^0+L_k-D_k^-&\le\mathcal B_k^{\rm ar}
                         \le\mathcal B_k^0+U_k+D_k^+.
 \end{aligned}}\label{eq:arithmeticinterval}
\end{equation}
The first interval is contained in the previous symmetric interval
because each $a_k^\pm\le2\Xi_{k,2q}$. The second evaluates its
allowances using the full finite source estimate. The exact two low
Gamma endpoints in JSA26--30 can be substituted before bounding;
this removes precisely their two truncation widths from the original
certificate with the same high-endpoint orders. All original mixed
covariance factors remain in that narrower interval.

The original amplification identities give, on either length-$q$ window,
\begin{equation}
 L_{h,k}^{2q}\le
 \frac{\omega_j^{\rm ar}}{\omega_i^{\rm ar}}
 \frac{V_i^{\rm ar}}{V_j^{\rm ar}},\qquad
 L_{h,k}\ge\frac\delta2 kq,
\end{equation}
with the separate first-admissible-degree formula at $i=q-1$.
The original HC5 lower bound remains $4q\log(D_hk)$ with the
same $D_h$. In particular the retained residual satisfies
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{\begin{aligned}
 \max\{0,\mathcal B_k^0+L_k-D_k^--4q\log(D_hk)\}
 &\le\mathcal B_k^{\rm ar}-4q\log(D_hk)\\
 &\le\mathcal B_k^0+U_k+D_k^+-4q\log(D_hk).
 \end{aligned}}
\end{equation}
This is the updated upper slack with the full Gamma return.

The original-degree estimate, with $p=8m-9/2$ and
$\eta=(p-1)/p$, is
\begin{equation}
 \frac{\Xi_{k,N}}{kq}
 =O_h\!\left(\frac{\log k}{k}
                  +\left(\frac{k\log k}{q}\right)^\eta\right)
 \quad(N=q-1,q,2q-1,2q).
\end{equation}
For $m\ge2$, retaining $q=(k+1)^2[1+k(m-1)]$ gives the precise
signed limits of the finite majorants
\begin{equation}
 \frac{D_k^-}{q\log k}\longrightarrow64m+245,
 \qquad \frac{D_k^+}{q\log k}\longrightarrow128m+490.
\end{equation}
Their proof is JSR18--21, including every finite $N$ factor.
For $m=1$, the current source bound instead retains
$\Xi_{k,N}/(kq)=O_h((\log k/k)^{5/7})$.
These statements replace the older rate at this receiving site;
they do not identify the signed Gamma term with the arithmetic defect.

A log-volume error $E_k$ changes a window exponential by factors
between $e^{-E_k/(2q)}$ and $e^{E_k/(2q)}$. Thus $o(q)$ gives a
factor tending to one and $o(q\log k)$ retains the leading logarithmic
threshold. The free summand has the sharper proved finite expansion
\begin{equation}
 C_{q,l}^{\rm free}=2l(l-\tfrac12)\log2
 -\frac{l(l-\tfrac12)(l+1/4)}q+R_{q,l},\quad
 0\le R_{q,l}\le\frac{l(l-\tfrac12)(14l^2+5l+3)}{16q^2}.
\end{equation}
The complete free-boundary proof below gives a second-order enclosure
and its constant terms at the same original degrees. Its nonzero
$q$-scale limit for simple quartets remains part of the exact return.
The remaining growing-family calculation concerns the relation-dependent
Schur term together with the original arithmetic deficit in the displayed
upper slack. Fixed-input convergence and the free summand alone do not
supply a sign for that entire expression.
